<%# readouts.ejs
     The station-bar readouts: what the poller is doing, how many watches
     are live, and how long until the next sweep.

     These live in the topbar, which no longer re-renders when you change
     tabs — so left alone they would be frozen at whatever they said when
     the tab was first opened, and the countdown in particular would sit
     at "due" for the rest of the session. Every fragment response carries
     this block back out of band, so the shell stays as current as the
     page under it.

     `oob` is the only difference between the two renders. It must be a
     TOP-LEVEL element of the fragment: htmx only looks for out-of-band
     markers among the response's own children. %>
<div class="chips" id="shellReadouts"<%- oob ? ' hx-swap-oob="true"' : '' %>>
  <%# THE CHIP PRINTS THE SNAPSHOT'S OWN LABEL.

      It used to carry its own vocabulary — a ternary that read
      "Sweeping" when sweeping, and otherwise guessed from the watch
      counts. That was fine while `sweeping` meant "the poller is on and
      somebody has a watch", and became wrong the moment it started
      meaning something precise: this process is WORKING right now.

      The result was a screenshot reading "Poller off" in the topbar
      while the card below it said "Standby — another process is
      crawling". Both were rendering the same snapshot by then; only one
      of them was rendering its LABEL. Every non-working state — standby,
      idle, behind — fell into the "Poller off" branch because that was
      the only word the ternary had left.

      So the fallbacks are gone. runtime.js names the state and this
      prints the name. A state it has never heard of renders as that
      state rather than as a guess. %>
  <%# Guarded, and the fallback is deliberately NOT cheerful. A page
      that forgets to pass the snapshot shows "Unknown" and a dark dot,
      never a green one — claiming health nobody measured is the exact
      bug this whole model replaced. %>
  <span class="chip"><span class="dot <%= (typeof pollerHealthy !== 'undefined' && pollerHealthy) ? 'live' : 'off' %> live-dot"></span>
    <b><%= typeof pollerLabel !== 'undefined' ? pollerLabel : 'Unknown' %></b></span>
  <span class="chip"><span class="k">Watches</span><b><%= activeCount %>/<%= watchCount %></b></span>
  <%# The countdown comes from the server. Deriving it from row
      elements meant it only worked on /watches, so the page people
      actually sit on showed "—" forever. %>
  <span class="chip"><span class="k">Next</span><b class="tnum" id="nextSweep"
    data-next-sweep="<%= nextSweepAt ? nextSweepAt : '' %>">—</b></span>
</div>
